WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.713
Runbook R08 is the last mile.

2
00:00:02.713 --> 00:00:07.530
An application that signs users in with
Entra ID but reaches the database with

3
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.200
a stored password has moved its front
door and left the back door where it was.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:18.500
Phase 1 inventories the LDAP-bind
dependency with the read-only D1.9 script.

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:26.131
It combines account heuristics with domain
controller evidence: event 4624 with

6
00:00:26.131 --> 00:00:28.824
logon type 8, a clear-text bind,

7
00:00:28.824 --> 00:00:33.762
and events 2887 and 2889 in
the Directory Service log.

8
00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:35.772
Event 2889 names each client,

9
00:00:35.772 --> 00:00:40.711
but only after the LDAP interface
diagnostic setting is raised to two,

10
00:00:40.711 --> 00:00:43.306
and nothing is logged retroactively,

11
00:00:43.306 --> 00:00:47.575
so start the window after the
change and set it back afterward.

12
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:50.945
D1.9 doesn't say which
instance an application uses,

13
00:00:50.945 --> 00:00:56.241
so the program's connection-plan function
joins it to the D1.8 audit, assigns each

14
00:00:56.241 --> 00:01:01.938
application a class from observable signals,
and emits the connection-string change.

15
00:01:01.938 --> 00:01:05.188
Phase 2 is the simplest
change and the most gated,

16
00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:09.250
and it's made in application
configuration, never by a script.

17
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:14.287
In production, name a specific mode, such
as Active Directory Managed Identity.

18
00:01:14.287 --> 00:01:17.645
The Default mode tries credential
providers in sequence,

19
00:01:17.645 --> 00:01:22.262
which slows the first connection and can
switch identity when the host changes.

20
00:01:22.262 --> 00:01:25.043
Service principal mode
takes its secret from

21
00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:27.750
protected configuration,
never from source.

22
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:32.688
Setting the mode turns on encryption, so
the server certificate must be trusted.

23
00:01:32.688 --> 00:01:37.386
On an Arc host the driver gets the machine's
token from the local metadata service,

24
00:01:37.386 --> 00:01:41.663
and the process must be in the hybrid
agent extension applications group.

25
00:01:41.663 --> 00:01:45.268
Every application on that host
is then the same principal,

26
00:01:45.268 --> 00:01:48.949
so give each its own service
principal where grants differ.

27
00:01:48.949 --> 00:01:53.989
Three gates before cutover: the Entra
login exists, the identity holds the right

28
00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:58.875
database role, and the change was tested
on a production-equivalent Arc stack.

29
00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:03.395
The audience is database.windows.net,
not the Azure Government one,

30
00:02:03.395 --> 00:02:07.175
and pooled applications use
the access-token callback.

31
00:02:07.175 --> 00:02:09.731
Rollback is the prior connection string,

32
00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:12.500
with the legacy login
disabled, not dropped.
